{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"trunk-group","type":"group","x":-30,"y":-40,"width":660,"height":6240,"color":"5","label":"MAIN TALK — follow 01 to 13 downward"},
		{"id":"data-group","type":"group","x":-800,"y":-40,"width":660,"height":6240,"color":"4","label":"SUPPORTING DATA — attached to the relevant beat"},
		{"id":"deviation-group","type":"group","x":770,"y":-40,"width":660,"height":6240,"color":"2","label":"OPTIONAL DEVIATIONS — replace material, never add time"},
		{"id":"entry","type":"text","x":-30,"y":-360,"width":660,"height":250,"color":"6","text":"# FROM OPCODE TO INTENT\n**PDF-aligned structure · 20 minutes · English**\n\nCyan trunk = spoken sequence.\nGreen branches = data and preparation.\nOrange branches = optional detours.\n\n[[Talk Brief|Read the complete enriched plan]]"},
		{"id":"t01","type":"text","x":0,"y":0,"width":600,"height":340,"color":"5","text":"## 01 · One task - five eras\n**00:00–01:10 · MAIN TALK**\n\nOne task, progressively less explicit machinery.\n\n[[Trunk/01 One task - five eras|Open this section]]"},
		{"id":"b01-support-0","type":"text","x":-770,"y":0,"width":600,"height":210,"color":"4","text":"### Run of Show\n**SUPPORTING DATA · from 01\n\nPDF timings, handoffs, and a two-minute recovery cut list.\n\n[[Run of Show|Read this branch]]"},
		{"id":"t02","type":"text","x":0,"y":480,"width":600,"height":340,"color":"5","text":"## 02 · Entropy - a useful wrong turn\n**01:10–02:10 · MAIN TALK**\n\nEntropy crossed out; semantic density, clearly labelled a metaphor.\n\n[[Trunk/02 Entropy - a useful wrong turn|Open this section]]"},
		{"id":"b02-support-0","type":"text","x":-770,"y":480,"width":600,"height":210,"color":"4","text":"### Parking Lot and Accuracy\n**SUPPORTING DATA · from 02\n\nKeep the metaphors; correct the mechanisms and the strength of the claims.\n\n[[Parking Lot and Accuracy|Read this branch]]"},
		{"id":"b02-deviation-0","type":"text","x":800,"y":480,"width":600,"height":210,"color":"2","text":"### B02 Shannon and units of meaning\n**OPTIONAL DEVIATION · from 02\n\nOptional intellectual detour: entropy, semantic density, function points.\n\n[[Branches/B02 Shannon and units of meaning|Read this branch]]"},
		{"id":"t03","type":"text","x":0,"y":960,"width":600,"height":340,"color":"5","text":"## 03 · When the program was the machine\n**02:10–03:30 · MAIN TALK**\n\nENIAC wiring, then a punched card.\n\n[[Trunk/03 When the program was the machine|Open this section]]"},
		{"id":"b03-support-0","type":"text","x":-770,"y":960,"width":600,"height":210,"color":"4","text":"### B03 Historical visuals\n**SUPPORTING DATA · from 03\n\nENIAC, punched cards, and where the PDF gets its historical imagery.\n\n[[Branches/B03 Historical visuals|Read this branch]]"},
		{"id":"t04","type":"text","x":0,"y":1440,"width":600,"height":340,"color":"5","text":"## 04 · Move the work into the interpreter\n**03:30–05:00 · MAIN TALK**\n\nWhat the human specifies versus what the receiving system supplies.\n\n[[Trunk/04 Move the work into the interpreter|Open this section]]"},
		{"id":"b04-support-0","type":"text","x":-770,"y":1440,"width":600,"height":210,"color":"4","text":"### B04 FORTRAN and abstract-machine sources\n**SUPPORTING DATA · from 04\n\nBackground sources for the compiler investment and Dijkstra staircase.\n\n[[Branches/B04 FORTRAN and abstract-machine sources|Read this branch]]"},
		{"id":"t05","type":"text","x":0,"y":1920,"width":600,"height":340,"color":"5","text":"## 05 · Every layer builds another machine\n**05:00–06:20 · MAIN TALK**\n\nCPU → instructions → runtime → language → framework → intent interpreter.\n\n[[Trunk/05 Every layer builds another machine|Open this section]]"},
		{"id":"b05-deviation-0","type":"text","x":800,"y":1920,"width":600,"height":210,"color":"2","text":"### B05 Intentional Programming before LLMs\n**OPTIONAL DEVIATION · from 05\n\nSimonyi as historical precedent, not the origin story of Liva.\n\n[[Branches/B05 Intentional Programming before LLMs|Read this branch]]"},
		{"id":"t06","type":"text","x":0,"y":2400,"width":600,"height":340,"color":"5","text":"## 06 · SQL - say what and delegate how\n**06:20–07:30 · MAIN TALK**\n\nThe query stays; execution machinery fades away.\n\n[[Trunk/06 SQL - say what and delegate how|Open this section]]"},
		{"id":"b06-deviation-0","type":"text","x":800,"y":2400,"width":600,"height":210,"color":"2","text":"### B06 LLVM and a language for models\n**OPTIONAL DEVIATION · from 06\n\nDirect low-level generation, compact typed languages, and var versus int.\n\n[[Branches/B06 LLVM and a language for models|Read this branch]]"},
		{"id":"t07","type":"text","x":0,"y":2880,"width":600,"height":340,"color":"6","text":"## 07 · Brooks spoils the ending\n**07:30–09:00 · MAIN TALK**\n\n“The hard thing about building software is deciding what one wants to say, not saying it.”\n\nBrooks · 1986 · “Artificial Intelligence”\n\n[[Trunk/07 Brooks spoils the ending|Open this section]]"},
		{"id":"b07-support-0","type":"text","x":-770,"y":2880,"width":600,"height":210,"color":"4","text":"### B07 Brooks exact quote and context\n**SUPPORTING DATA · from 07\n\nVerified verbatim in the September 1986 report, section 4.3.\n\n[[Branches/B07 Brooks exact quote and context|Read this branch]]"},
		{"id":"t08","type":"text","x":0,"y":3360,"width":600,"height":340,"color":"5","text":"## 08 · The short prompt has a long context\n**09:00–10:40 · MAIN TALK**\n\nA short request draws on a large shared dictionary.\n\nModel knowledge + repository + examples + tools + tests.\n\nUseful interpretation is not lossless decompression.\n\n[[Trunk/08 The short prompt has a long context|Open this section]]"},
		{"id":"b08-support-0","type":"text","x":-770,"y":3360,"width":600,"height":210,"color":"4","text":"### Source Ideas\n**SUPPORTING DATA · from 08\n\nProvenance and how the co-host discussion enriches the PDF.\n\n[[Source Ideas|Read this branch]]"},
		{"id":"b08-deviation-0","type":"text","x":800,"y":3360,"width":600,"height":210,"color":"2","text":"### B08 Semantic representations\n**OPTIONAL DEVIATION · from 08\n\nContext-sensitive meaning, autoencoders, and why coordinates are not labels.\n\n[[Branches/B08 Semantic representations|Read this branch]]"},
		{"id":"b08-deviation-1","type":"text","x":800,"y":3595,"width":600,"height":210,"color":"2","text":"### B08 CSharp AST experiment\n**OPTIONAL DEVIATION · from 08\n\nA research proposal about code representations, with no claimed results.\n\n[[Branches/B08 CSharp AST experiment|Read this branch]]"},
		{"id":"t09","type":"text","x":0,"y":3840,"width":600,"height":340,"color":"5","text":"## 09 · Freedom is a bug - constraints narrow the options\n**10:40–12:40 · MAIN TALK**\n\nBroad cone of plausible outcomes → narrower acceptable region.\n\n[[Trunk/09 Freedom is a bug - constraints narrow the options|Open this section]]"},
		{"id":"b09-support-0","type":"text","x":-770,"y":3840,"width":600,"height":210,"color":"4","text":"### B09 Constraints comparison and experiment caveats\n**SUPPORTING DATA · from 09\n\nPrepared screenshot comparison and the limits of a constraints claim.\n\n[[Branches/B09 Constraints comparison and experiment caveats|Read this branch]]"},
		{"id":"t10","type":"text","x":0,"y":4320,"width":600,"height":340,"color":"5","text":"## 10 · Reference beats description\n**12:40–14:20 · MAIN TALK**\n\nA paragraph of styling instructions versus one concrete repository reference.\n\n[[Trunk/10 Reference beats description|Open this section]]"},
		{"id":"b10-support-0","type":"text","x":-770,"y":4320,"width":600,"height":210,"color":"4","text":"### B10 Context and executable boundaries\n**SUPPORTING DATA · from 10\n\nReferences, tool contracts, maintained intent, and test limits.\n\n[[Branches/B10 Context and executable boundaries|Read this branch]]"},
		{"id":"t11","type":"text","x":0,"y":4800,"width":600,"height":340,"color":"5","text":"## 11 · The bottleneck moved\n**14:20–16:50 · MAIN TALK**\n\n2025 measured slowdown and mistaken perception; then the mandatory 2026 caveat.\n\n[[Trunk/11 The bottleneck moved|Open this section]]"},
		{"id":"b11-support-0","type":"text","x":-770,"y":4800,"width":600,"height":210,"color":"4","text":"### B11 METR evidence and limits\n**SUPPORTING DATA · from 11\n\nThe 2025 result and February 2026 update must travel together.\n\n[[Branches/B11 METR evidence and limits|Read this branch]]"},
		{"id":"t12","type":"text","x":0,"y":5280,"width":600,"height":340,"color":"5","text":"## 12 · Understanding is still expensive\n**16:50–18:10 · MAIN TALK**\n\nExecution becomes easier; evaluation still needs judgment.\n\n[[Trunk/12 Understanding is still expensive|Open this section]]"},
		{"id":"b12-support-0","type":"text","x":-770,"y":5280,"width":600,"height":210,"color":"4","text":"### B12 Learning and evaluation evidence\n**SUPPORTING DATA · from 12\n\n50% versus 67%; short-term learning, not a universal loss of skill.\n\n[[Branches/B12 Learning and evaluation evidence|Read this branch]]"},
		{"id":"b12-deviation-0","type":"text","x":800,"y":5280,"width":600,"height":210,"color":"2","text":"### B12 Leaky abstractions\n**OPTIONAL DEVIATION · from 12\n\nA login request as the short route to a long technical fall.\n\n[[Branches/B12 Leaky abstractions|Read this branch]]"},
		{"id":"t13","type":"text","x":0,"y":5760,"width":600,"height":340,"color":"5","text":"## 13 · Intent is the new working unit\n**18:10–20:00 · MAIN TALK**\n\nVoice → questions → agreed intent → intent areas → agents → verification.\n\n**Less code. More meaning. More responsibility.**\n\n[[Trunk/13 Intent is the new working unit|Open this section]]"},
		{"id":"b13-support-0","type":"text","x":-770,"y":5760,"width":600,"height":210,"color":"4","text":"### B13 Liva process and analyst role\n**SUPPORTING DATA · from 13\n\nThe co-host contribution: maintain intent and a checked path to implementation.\n\n[[Branches/B13 Liva process and analyst role|Read this branch]]"},
		{"id":"b13-deviation-0","type":"text","x":800,"y":5760,"width":600,"height":210,"color":"2","text":"### Agent Hypothesis\n**OPTIONAL DEVIATION · from 13\n\nAgents by end-to-end scenario rather than technical job title.\n\n[[Agent Hypothesis|Read this branch]]"},
		{"id":"b13-deviation-1","type":"text","x":800,"y":5995,"width":600,"height":210,"color":"2","text":"### Notes App Demo\n**OPTIONAL DEVIATION · from 13\n\nYour notes-app example, preserved as an alternative worked scenario.\n\n[[Notes App Demo|Read this branch]]"}
	],
